# Tool attributes, which are the DEFAULTS FOR THE NEXT PLACEMENT rather than a property of
# any component. Both sides write the currently selected tool's own attribute set -- Java the
# library instance, this port the canvas tool the controller upgraded it into -- and then place
# twice, so the file shows both that the attributes reached the first component and that they
# survived to the second. A tool whose attributes are rebuilt per placement writes two bare
# gates here.
tool	add:AND Gate
toolattr	facing	north
toolattr	inputs	3
click	300	200
click	400	200
